t never asked about the boundary). 241	- No round cap: iterate until achieved or until the harness turn budget is exhausted; without achievement → honestly write `final` entry (verdict not achieved, recommendation explains); no fabricated achievement. Negative results are results — the paper honestly reports "not achieved within budget" as far more valuable than beautifying data. 242	- `real_compute: false` → closing skips `run-orca`/`run-md` true-compute endorsement (`endorse` entry honestly records skip reason; no fabricated DFT/MD values). 243	 244	## 3. Forbidden Actions and Anti-Patterns (iron rules) 245	 246	- ❌ Fabricating simulation values: no metric may be written for an unexecuted command 247	- ❌ Skipping screening layers straight to true compute: `run-orca`/`run-cp2k`/`run-qe`/`run-md` forbidden inside the funnel 248	- ❌ Declaring completion without achieving: must fall back and retry until achieved or budget exhausted 249	- ❌ Modifying JSON intermediate file contents: read-only, no editing 250	- ❌ Omitting commands: every step's command must be really executed and its output read before proceeding 251	 252	Supplementary discipline: 253	 254	- The iron rule "do not edit JSON intermediate files" refers to **command output artifacts** (`--out` files and workspace artifacts) as read-only; agent-built **input files** (run-pyamm params, run-md box, etc.) are new files, allowed to write 255	- Failures recorded honestly: simulation failure, DFT non-convergence, candidate eliminated — all written verbatim to log and report; no beautification or concealment 256	- **Reports prefer tables/figures**: candidate comparisons in evaluate's `comparison` table, funnel dispositions in funnel's `dispositions` table, diagnosis in a one-sentence `note` — avoid long prose paragraphs in the log 257	 258	## 4. Simulation Library Command Quick Reference 259	 260	Invocation (Bash tool, repo root): `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m bda <subcommand> ...`. **Full parameters/IO schemas/erro